   "subject": "Re: Error message",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Not sure what the problem is, but it looks like these are just the same set of predictors predicting multiple outcomes.  Other than not getting estimates of the residual correlations among latent responses assumed to underlie outcomes, you can get the same estimated effects from the glm() function running one outcome at a time.<div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792426885680000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1OPBrFiWe3Y5PoBHI7xxuZ\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
